Why MIT: this licence is inherited, not chosen

ipnx-v12 is a derivative work of Plan 9. Its kernel is Plan 9's, modified, and
its userland derives from Plan 9's own — so the licence comes from upstream.

Nokia Bell Labs transferred the Plan 9 copyright to the Plan 9 Foundation on
23 March 2021, and the Foundation relicensed all previous editions under the
MIT licence. plan9port carries the same terms, and APE ships with Plan 9 and so
falls under the same transfer.

Plan 9-derived material remains the copyright of the Plan 9 Foundation and
carries its own notice. MIT requires that notice be reproduced with any copy or
substantial portion, so it travels with the code rather than being replaced by
the grant above. The copyright line above claims only this repository's own
content — at present the documentation, and the kernel modifications, file
servers and host application as they are added.

Research Unix is a separate estate and is NOT covered here

The Tenth Edition personality is designed against Research Unix, which is
subject to Nokia's 2017 covenant rather than to a licence. No Research Unix
source is copied into this repository; the V10 measurements in RESEARCH.md are
recorded as data, taken in the parent repository
(https://github.com/ChristineTham/ipnx), where that estate is reasoned about.

A V12 image mixes the two estates. Per docs/v12-plan.md that is answered before
code, not after, and this file will need revisiting when it is.
